Subject: [PATCH] x86_64: instrument hidden unwind assembly entry points for IBT
Origin: other, Peios catalogue qualification review
Upstream-Status: Pending [manual assembly must follow the native CET contract]

Rust compiler CET flags cannot instrument global_asm bodies. Add ENDBR64
at the handwritten unwind entry points, retaining hidden visibility and
the existing fatal-personality/abort behavior. ENDBR64 is a compatible NOP
on x86_64 processors without IBT. No ELF property notes are forced.

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -65,6 +65,7 @@
     ".globl rust_eh_personality",
     ".type rust_eh_personality, @function",
     "rust_eh_personality:",
+    "endbr64",
     "mov eax, 3",
     "ret",
     ".size rust_eh_personality, . - rust_eh_personality",
